    "full_details": "Notices\nThe \"Guardians of the Golden Temple Order\" is here! One ★4 Skill Record is guaranteed on Step 3!\nShop\n2025-09-10 17:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nYuuki, Asuna, Leafa, and Silica are safeguarding a glorious temple from ancient times as new ★4 Skill Records!\nThe \"\nGuardians of the Golden Temple Order\n\" is here! Get one ★4 Skill Record guaranteed on Step 3!\nThe 6% total drop rate does not include the guaranteed ★4 Skill Record, and new ★4 Skill Records are featured Skill Records with high drop rates!\nOn Step 1, you can get 11 Orders for 1,250 Arcana Gems!\nOne ★4 Skill Record is guaranteed on Step 3!\n【New ★4 Skill Records】\n★4[Royal Authority] Yuuki\nWeapon Type\n1H Sword\nSkill Name\nShadow Pierce\nSP Cost\n26\nElement\nSlash/\nDark\nSkill Cool Time\n14.0\nSwitch Gauge\n45\nBreak Gauge\n20\nSkill Effect\n1610% damage (5x hit/All Foes)[Front/Long/Mid]/▲▲▲[Bonus] Damage +100% to enemies when using dark skills./[Bonus] When equipping 3 or more of Yuuki's Skill Records in the same set, Attack +1000.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nMOD Skill\n★4[Queen of the Sun] Asuna\nWeapon Type\n1H Rapier\nSkill Name\nBrown Pulsar\nSP Cost\n26\nElement\nThrust/\nEarth\nSkill Cool Time\n14.0\nSwitch Gauge\n80\nBreak Gauge\n40\nSkill Effect\n2250% damage (Single Foe)[Motion Range]/[Earth Pile/Buff] Earth element damage +1% per stack (Stack3) during 20 sec./[Earth Pile/Buff] When the target is hit using the Switch, Earth element damage +1% per stack (Stack9) during 20 sec.\n*More than regular increase in switch gauge.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nChain Skill\nActivates a chain state that turns all Chain Skills and sword skills with Limit Break +10 into Switch for a certain duration when a Super Chain is activated.\n・Super Chain effect (activates 1x)\nEarth damage +50% when using earth skills.\nAttack +1000 while the buff to raise earth damage is in effect.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\n★4[Underworld Arbiter] Leafa\nSkill Name\nPower Rise/Enhance Attack/Halo\nAttack\n55\nDefense\n30\nHP\n2500\nSkill Effect\n[Power Rise 4] Attack +900./[Enhance Attack 4] Attack +15%./[Halo 3] Defense -30% and during the buff effect for increased max HP the hit rate -30%\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nChain Skill\nExtra effect time 7.5 sec.\nFor each 1 equipped in the same set, switch damage during the chain state increases, and the effect time is extended.\n・Effect during Chain\nDeals +5% Earth element's damage to enemy.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\n★4[Guardian of the Skies] Silica\nWeapon Type\nDagger\nSkill Name\nFlood Spin\nSP Cost\n26\nElement\nSlash/\nWater\nSkill Cool Time\n14.0\nSwitch Gauge\n96\nBreak Gauge\n33\nSkill Effect\n2170% damage (6x hit/Single Foe)[Center/Arc/Mid]/[Aqua Pile/Buff] Water element damage +1% per stack (Stack3) during 20 sec./[Aqua Pile/Buff] When the target is hit using the Switch, water element damage +1% per stack (Stack9) during 20 sec.\n* More than regular increase in switch gauge.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\nChain Skill\nActivates a chain state that turns all Chain Skills and sword skills with Limit Break +10 into Switch for a certain duration when a Super Chain is activated.\n・Super Chain effect (activates 1x)\nWater damage +50% when using water skills.\nAttack +1000 while the buff to raise water damage is in effect.\n*Evolving & Maximum Breakthrough\n- Duration\nAfter the September 10, 2025 (Wed) maintenance - October 10, 2025 (Fri) 16:59 (JST/UTC+9)\n- Step Offers/Details\nStep Number\nOffers\nDetails\nSTEP1\n1,250 Arcana Gems\n1.3% total Drop Rate for featured Skill Records\nSTEP2\n2,500 Arcana Gems\n1.3% total Drop Rate for featured Skill Records\nSTEP3\n2,500 Arcana Gems\nOne ★4 Skill Record guaranteed!\n1.3% total Drop Rate for featured Skill Records\n- Important\nPlease see the in-game Order details for the entire lineup.\nAll Steps are 11 Orders.\nThe Drop Rates for each rarity may vary depending on the Step. For more information, tap Order Details/Drop Rate.\nAfter Step 3, you will return to Step 1.\nPlease be aware that the event period may change without prior notice.\nGo to Notice List"
